course: dictionary
lesson: 689
title: Banana in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A banana is a long, curved fruit with a yellow skin that you peel. Inside, it is soft and sweet. Context tells you which meaning of a word a sentence uses, so read the words around banana before you decide.
explain: «A banana is a good snack, but it does not prevent cramp in sport for most people.» Snack is a clue: you eat a snack between meals. So banana means the fruit here, not the plant.
explain: «He packs bananas, sugar-cane and melons.» Packing things into a bag tells you bananas are food you can carry. The -s on bananas means more than one banana.
explain: Sometimes the clues point somewhere else entirely. «Go bananas» is a phrase that means to go wild with excitement, so the fruit is not involved at all. Always ask: does this sentence make sense with the fruit meaning?
fact: A banana is a long, curved fruit with a yellow skin that you peel.
fact: A banana plant is the large plant that bananas grow on, in a bunch.
fact: As a banana ripens, starch turns into sugar and the skin browns.
fact: Bananas grow in warm places and turn from green to yellow as they ripen.
fact: «Go bananas» means go wild with excitement, so it is an idiom, not a fruit.
exercise: «As a banana ripens, starch turns into sugar and the skin browns.» What does ripens mean? | Gets bigger and heavier | Is peeled and eaten | Falls off the plant | *Becomes ready to eat, growing softer and sweeter
exercise: A bunch has 6 bananas. How many bananas are in 3 bunches? | 3 | 9 | 6 | *18
exercise: Mia says «the kids will go bananas» means they must eat a fruit. What does go bananas mean? | Grow a banana tree in the garden | *Go wild with excitement | Peel a banana very fast | Eat only fruit for a week
test: «A banana is a good snack, but it does not prevent cramp in sport for most people.» In this sentence, what is a banana? | *A fruit you eat as a snack | A kind of cramp | A type of sport | A plant with big leaves
test: Bananas turn from green to yellow as they ripen. What colour is a banana that is ripe? | Red | *Yellow | Green | Blue
exam: «Some surprises hide in the kitchen: a potato is a swollen stem, not a root; a banana is a berry but a strawberry is not.» According to the sentence, which is true? | A peanut is a fruit | A strawberry is a berry | A potato is a root | *A banana is a berry
